1
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Some people get into trouble no matter what they wear.

2
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Striptease is a comedy, crime, drama film directed by Andrew Bergman.

3
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Bounced from her job, Erin Grant needs money if she's to have
any chance of winning back custody of her child.

4
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
But, eventually, she must confront the naked truth: to take on
the system, she'll have to take it all off.

5
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Erin strips to conquer, but she faces unintended circumstances when a hound dog of a Congressman zeroes
in on her and sharpens the shady tools at his fingertips, including blackmail and murder.

6
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Erin Grant, played by Demi Moore.

7
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:21,000
David Dilbeck, played by Burt Reynolds.

8
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Lt. Al Garcia, played by Armand Assante.

9
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:51,000
Shad, played by Ving Rhames.

10
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Darrell Grant, played by Robert Patrick.

11
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
Malcolm Moldovsky, played by Paul Guilfoyle.

12
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Striptease is a 1996 American black comedy film written, co-produced and directed by Andrew Bergman,
and starring Demi Moore, Armand Assante, Ving Rhames, Robert Patrick and Burt Reynolds.

13
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
Based on Carl Hiaasen's 1993 best-selling novel of the same name, the film centers on an FBI
secretary-turned-stripper who becomes involved in both a child-custody dispute and corrupt politics.

14
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
Moore was paid a then-unprecedented $12.5 million to star in Striptease,
making her the highest-paid film actress up to that time.

15
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
Released theatrically on June 28, 1996, by Columbia Pictures and produced by Castle Rock Entertainment with a $50
million budget, the film grossed $33 million domestically (47th place) and $113 million worldwide.

16
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
It was somewhat more successful in the subsequent video rental market.

17
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:51,000
However, it was panned by critics and won six Golden
Raspberry Awards including Worst Picture.

18
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:36,000
The film explores themes of dance, police, blackmail, striptease, satire.

19
01:49:15,000 --> 01:49:21,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
